              "before": "# Sequence hover highlighting\n\nNative Turbo coverage uses `NativeSequenceSelection.ts` for blue selection only. Complementary filters copy Mapillary's native line/circle styles, preserving other coverage paints, dimensions, opacity, stroke, zoom limits and user filters. SceneView prepares a complete replacement coverage layer while the displayed coverage remains attached. MapView keeps its existing native selection update path. Buffered replacements are committed only after their layer view and first paints are ready; 2D hover also keeps its predecessor through the SDK tile fade. Coverage references and display anchors retain their logical source identity across swaps. Superseded work is cancelled and its staged layer is destroyed; failed preparation leaves the displayed layer intact. SceneView still avoids individual style-layer updates, which can lose line/circle render buckets.\n\nHover remains a separate neon green (`#00ff88`) native tile sequence line, now 6 pixels wide instead of 5. It does not turn circles blue or replace the selected sequence. Moving between points in the same sequence reuses the existing hover style. A different hover sequence is prepared separately and replaces the previous green renderer only when ready; mouseout cancels staged work immediately. The main Turbo map does not reconstruct sequence overview lines from image coordinates: cached/completed API route geometry is retained for the minimap. `tests/nativeSequenceSelection.test.cjs` covers these contracts, including asynchronous SceneView updates.\n\n`SequenceHoverHighlight.ts` owns one reusable vector-tile layer and the last hovered sequence ID. `widget.tsx` forwards hover intent and supplies current host dependencies. The line-only style is colocated with its lifecycle owner; this layer does not draw image circles or change active-sequence point membership.\n\n`update` ignores identical IDs, hides the layer on mouseout, and creates it lazily on the first nonempty hover. Later changes reuse the layer through `loadStyle`, retaining the style-property fallback for older SDKs. Detached layers are reattached at the existing coverage-relative index. The host supplies the current access token; no token is embedded in source files.\n\nBoth cleanup paths cancel staged work. `detach` removes and destroys the displayed hover renderer during widget cleanup; `reset` also clears its displayed/desired identity during view transfer. Aborted preparations cannot reattach a stale renderer.\n\nThe owner adds no Graph calls, watchers, timers, playback callbacks or point graphics. Highlight tiles retain the existing source URL and zoom limits. `tests/sequenceHoverHighlight.test.cjs` covers reuse, style contents, hide/show, reattachment, the SDK fallback, cleanup and runtime forwarding. Experience Builder still needs visual checks for hover transitions and layer order in 2D and 3D.\n\n## Image-first clicks\n\nAn exact hovered image starts `moveTo` before a separate coordinate query or route preparation. Tracking is seeded with the requested identity first, and coordinates come from the viewer image when available. Blue selection preparation is deferred while the image is opening. Once the viewer opens, the image-loading state clears independently of optional location or route metadata. A stale viewer event from a previous click cannot cancel the latest click. Regional line clicks still resolve the nearest image ID first.\n\n`tests/preparedVectorTileLayer.test.cjs` verifies readiness/cancellation/failure ownership; `tests/imageFirstSelection.test.cjs` verifies image, metadata and route ordering plus rapid-click guards.\n",
